@startuml
title Client Sessions: a retry across a leader change (§8)
skinparam defaultFontSize 10

participant "RaftClient\n(clientId=c, seq=7)" as C
participant "Leader A" as A
participant "Leader B\n(after election)" as B
participant "StateMachine\n(every server)" as SM

C -> A: Submit(cmd, client_id=c,\n  sequence=7, acked=6)
A -> A: append LogEntry(cmd, c, 7, acked=6)
note over A, B: entry replicated and committed
A -> SM: sessions.begin(c, 7) = NEW\napply(cmd) -> r\nsessions.record(c, 7, r)
A -x C: response lost\n(leader A crashes)

== Leader change ==
note over B: B applied the same entry from its log:\nits session table already holds (c, 7) -> r

C -> B: Submit(cmd, client_id=c,\n  sequence=7, acked=6)\n(same tag, the retry)
B -> B: append LogEntry(cmd, c, 7, acked=6)
note over B: committed like any other entry
B -> SM: sessions.begin(c, 7) = DUPLICATE\nstate machine is NOT called
B --> C: SubmitResponse(result = r)

== Next command ==
C -> B: Submit(cmd2, client_id=c,\n  sequence=8, acked=7)
B -> SM: sessions.begin(c, 8, acked=7)\ndrops the result held for 7\napply(cmd2)
B --> C: SubmitResponse(result = r2)
@enduml
